$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 11/Surveillance concepts

::EPI-W11-001::Which phrase best captures public-health surveillance? {
=Ongoing systematic collection, analysis, interpretation and dissemination of health data for action#Correct.
~A one-time research survey only#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Direct treatment of every reported patient#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Any database containing health information#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 11/Surveillance types

::EPI-W11-002::A health department routinely receives reports without actively calling every facility. What type is this? {
=Passive surveillance#Correct.
~Active surveillance#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Randomised surveillance#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Case-control surveillance#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

::EPI-W11-003::Selected clinics agree to report all cases of a condition to track trends. What approach is this? {
=Sentinel surveillance#Correct.
~Census#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Case-control study#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Cluster trial#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

::EPI-W11-004::A system monitors symptom patterns before specific diagnoses are confirmed. What approach is this? {
=Syndromic surveillance#Correct.
~Retrospective cohort#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Experimental surveillance#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Cross-sectional intervention#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 11/Attributes

::EPI-W11-005::What does surveillance sensitivity describe? {
=Ability to detect true cases or events of interest#Correct.
~Proportion of detected alerts that are true#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Speed of data transmission only#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Willingness of facilities to report#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

::EPI-W11-006::What does predictive value positive describe in surveillance? {
=Proportion of detected cases or alerts that are truly cases or events#Correct.
~Proportion of true cases detected#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Proportion of noncases correctly ignored#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
~Number of facilities reporting#Review surveillance purpose and outbreak-investigation logic.
}

